SOAPBOX: Casual operating from modest home station to see how things were this year...1632Z-1846Z, 2100Z-2120Z, then 0215Z-0700Z, while binge watching Danish TV with subtitles.
SOAPBOX: Breakdown was 97 FT4 and 41 FT8. Somewhat more variety of mults on FT8, but waiting for it reminds me of a trip to the DMV.  Rotated between bands and modes, occasionally going to the non-contest watering hole when things got slow.
SOAPBOX: Considered setting up         another computer         for      SO2R,            but      there
SOAPBOX: General impression is that people didn't spread out enough. Activity was decent and included a lot of well-known contesters. Not much EU when I was operating, though saw a few W7s working them.  Was pleased to work several HS's on 20m at mid-day.
SOAPBOX: I still wish a new digital mode could be designed specifically with contesting in mind, preferably without fixed time slots.
